# Cloudflare Workers static-assets deploy (wrangler deploy) scans the
# entire repo checkout by default -- without this file it was uploading
# .git/ internals (config, objects, logs) and Wrangler's own build-time
# scratch files as if they were public site content (found 2026-09-01,
# first deploy). Nothing sensitive was in .git/config (just the public
# GitHub remote URL), but none of this belongs on the live site.
.git
.wrangler
_build
wrangler.jsonc
.gitignore
.assetsignore
